      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;introduction&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Introduction&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#introduction&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I was recently playing with around with &lt;a href=&#34;https://flutter.dev/multi-platform/web&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Flutter web&lt;/a&gt; and was wondering how I would go about getting it to work with &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.djangoproject.com/&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Django&lt;/a&gt; and deploying them together.&#xA;The application I decided to test this with is a kanban type application, so flutter would be used to build the frontend UI and Django would provide the REST API.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;development&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Development&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#development&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;directory-structure&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Directory Structure&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#directory-structure&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Our project directory structure will looks very similar to the traditional Django project structure.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
